node_modules/
dist/
*.log
dollhouse/lib/

# Rust core build dir
scher-core/target/
scher-core-wasm/target/
scher-epistemology/target/
# wasm-pack output — COMMITTED, not ignored (Hallie's call 2026-07-30: "commit
# it for now"). 153KB of compiled kernel + generated .d.ts. Committing it means
# a fresh checkout has the compiled reads with NO Rust toolchain — only
# maintainers need rustup/wasm-pack, which is the normal deal for any compiled
# dependency. wasm-pack writes its own pkg/.gitignore containing `*` (its
# default assumption is that you publish rather than commit); that file is
# force-added below so the bytes actually land.
#
# REBUILD after touching any Rust: cd scher-core-wasm && wasm-pack build --target web --release
# The committed bytes are an artifact and CAN go stale — if they disagree with
# the source, the conformance corpus is what catches it (the wasm replay in
# test/conformance.wasm.test.ts runs against these exact bytes).
src/*.js
# generated by dollhouse/build.mjs — never committed; the play-tests are the truth
dollhouse/index.html
examples/*/node_modules
examples/*/dist
